From 2324d08980c9da185099d001e354b31598a39fe9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "claude[bot]" <41898282+claude[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 06:14:11 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] Add a deck-mounted stirrer instrument type and a `stir`
 protocol command

Approach 1 of vertical-cloud-lab/byu-vcl#133: a magnetic stirrer is declared
under `instruments:` like any other device, and its registry type says where
it is mounted.

- registry.yaml: a `stirrer` type with `mount: deck`. `mount` is `head` (the
  default) or `deck`; registry.py validates it and adds get_mount() and
  is_deck_mounted(). The gantry loader copies it onto each instance, and
  base_instrument.is_deck_mounted_instrument() is the one predicate head
  geometry asks. It compares the value, so test doubles and MagicMocks stay
  head-mounted, as every instrument was before.
- A deck-mounted entry carries a driver and a port only. The loader refuses
  a non-zero offset_x, offset_y or depth on it; its place on the deck goes in
  the deck file (for now as a `wall`, an obstacle).
- instruments/stirrer/: StirrerInstrument with two high-level calls,
  set_stirrer_params(rpm, seconds=None) and get_stirrer_params(), plus
  stop() (set_stirrer_params(0)) and wait_until_stopped(timeout).
  Vendors:
  * pawduino: the stir module on the PANDA Arduino, over the shared
    PawduinoLink (it shares the board with the capper and the pipette).
    set_stirrer_params sends firmware command `30,<rpm>[,<seconds>]` and
    get_stirrer_params sends `31`. connect() checks that the firmware has
    them. Optional `status_poll_s` logs `31` while it stirs.
  * mock: an in-memory model of the firmware's ramp, for --mock and tests.
- protocol_engine/commands/stir.py: `stir` with `instrument`, `rpm` (0
  stops), optional `seconds` (the stirrer stops itself after that long), and
  `wait`, which defaults to true when `seconds` is given.
- disconnect_instruments() stops every stirrer before disconnecting, as it
  already turns every light off, so an aborted run never leaves one spinning.
- Skipped for deck-mounted instruments: gantry bounds, home poses, the setup
  summary, the calibration CLIs, and head moves (_resolve_instrument refuses
  one; InstrumentedGantry.head_instruments lists the rest).

The protocol names the stirrer, not the vial on it, so CubOS does not yet
know what is being stirred and enforces no interlock. That is left to the
deck-instrument design that follows this.

The firmware commands are in byu-vcl's cubos/firmware/panda-arduino-
stirrer.patch. With the 496819c form of this change, the CubXL ran a 45-step
protocol on 2026-11-17 and 2026-11-18 that stirred one vial while working on
another.

Refs vertical-cloud-lab/byu-vcl#133

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
